    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "611-613"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "619-630"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2437-2440"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2442-2445"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2447-2448"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2643-2646"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Status Register A is read-only and monitors the state of the interrupt pin and several disk interface pins.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "597-600",
       "sha": "68494139d8abe00298ac00acad4aee8082022a7bebcc70cf18033ee0d0c36b2c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The register is part of the PS/2 register set and is not accessible in PC-AT mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "597-602",
       "sha": "10d5dd3e66bf0756fb3d265100e9ef256e68613e147917de236bcccd3aa90571"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Its bits are INT PENDING (7), DRV2 (6), STEP (5), TRK0 (4), HDSEL (3), INDX (2), WP (1) and DIR (0); after reset STEP, HDSEL and DIR are 0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "606-610",
       "sha": "380d8b94da2f3019c8c28a0e9e2f9247012023f995bc8ae1c6e840cfafd4eb36"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "INT PENDING lets software monitor the INTERRUPT pin, and the marked bits reflect drive signals on the cable independently of INVERT.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "611-613",
       "sha": "3d739b0c94150114d22d4807a92db2715e227689ebac203ba5f28be5b3c8d927"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In Model 30 mode bits 0 to 4 are inverted, DRQ (printed DRO, bit 6) monitors the DMA request, and STEP (bit 5) is latched with the step output.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "619-630",
       "sha": "30d3f97b94cbeba2e9b0d17488e672dc4d2ecf974cea301f391a6bbf141070a2"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "2",
     "text": "In PC-AT mode the emulator's read handler leaves the case and returns 0xFF, so the register reads all ones.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2643-2646",
       "sha": "0b9867d008d021113870c722d5e1071e9d336260786ceacf571d0c69f8ae31a3"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2678",
       "sha": "241fe285b912b96cb626e2777b402f683b760b7d92a86fbe3ccc7cc07b3769b5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "3",
     "text": "Bit 7 is the interrupt state; bit 6 set without a second drive, bit 4 off track 0, bits 2 to 0 one, bits 5 and 3 zero.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2447-2448",
       "sha": "a264d06131e493b49a7b5c8b9beb41ae4ce287d62b352d83af932f53fb5fcbef"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "5",
     "text": "In Model 30 mode bit 7 carries the interrupt; the emulator returns bit 4 only at track 0, 1 in bits 3 and 0, and 0 in DRQ and STEP.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2442-2445",
       "sha": "2a07c076850eb9c82d99e3e05196c2bf14b399a5601ac1e2fdc7e35b1cbbcade"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2437-2440",
     "as": "structure"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2447-2448",
     "as": "agrees",
     "row": "4"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x01",
   "name": "status register B",
   "aliases": [
    "SRB",
    "status register B"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "631-638"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "646-655"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2452-2453"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2455-2459"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2461-2462"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2647-2648"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Status Register B is read-only and monitors the state of several disk interface pins.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "631-632",
       "sha": "56a9f8a0fc10f00d14c39b7b68d72b2e0de94ec354b5ff1a90cc7f12f2c310e8"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "It is part of the PS/2 register set and is not accessible in PC-AT mode.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "632-633",
       "sha": "09134e61ad74371bb1004a89148facbe4a5314cf4a46fc58414dda101794d135"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In PS/2 mode bits 7 and 6 are 1, bit 5 is drive select 0, bits 4 and 3 toggle, and bits 2 to 0 are WE and motor enables.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "634-638",
       "sha": "0a2ab2144c7a34ba5abae4c9b04147400c8eef13a329393692cf7e346df430f9"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "In Model 30 mode bits 0, 1, 5 and 6 return the decoded drive selects, and bits 2 to 4 are set by edges and cleared by a DIR read.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "646-655",
       "sha": "a8ed96d662a63bddf46888b269b2e949d2c9137d2758ed5b526d9b52bca1dd8f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "2",
     "text": "In PC-AT mode the emulator's read handler leaves the case and returns 0xFF, so the register reads all ones.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2647-2648",
       "sha": "489809b32b4356e31bf66a81c988dc8567f4b8f496ecdac18089ad1db318e856"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2678",
       "sha": "241fe285b912b96cb626e2777b402f683b760b7d92a86fbe3ccc7cc07b3769b5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "3",
     "text": "Bits 7 and 6 are 1, bit 5 comes from the DOR's drive select, bits 1 and 0 from its motor enables, and WRDATA, RDDATA and WE read 0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2461-2462",
       "sha": "84fa9da66bf1010ef77167d32940e6de37c8bd16e89d3369836e97c83a4c5e0b"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "4",
     "text": "The FDC returns the negated drive selects in bits 6, 5, 1 and 0 and 0 in bits 4, 3 and 2, so no edge is latched.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2455-2459",
       "sha": "425eadbf0ac56642bda74c6f282039b71f7db4df41ff634335ad53802cae9d3a"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "closed": [
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2452-2453",
     "as": "structure"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "key": "0x02",
   "name": "DOR",
   "aliases": [
    "digital output register",
    "digital output port"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "656-667"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "674-677"
    },
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
     "lines": "682-685"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "1143-1144"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "1146-1157"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "1161-1162"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "1164-1169"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "1177-1180"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "1182-1185"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2595-2596"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
     "lines": "2650-2651"
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The Digital Output Register holds the drive select and motor enable bits, a reset bit and a DMA GATE bit.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "656-657",
       "sha": "353587c7e8651994f4442ad4a19a2f8aac7c7ea8473b575152e215ddb2cff87a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bits 7 to 4 are the motor enables and bits 1 and 0 the drive selects; a set bit is active and one drive is selected at a time.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "658-667",
       "sha": "1b9e0442c26df4781b4d377e87c46816748e0ab7d707fd8b0e46315ee81a21e0"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The DMA GATE bit works only in PC-AT and Model 30 modes: low, it tristates INT and DRQ and disables DACK and TC; in PS/2 mode it has no effect.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "674-677",
       "sha": "16cd4db5bdd564f2bf292f41110f1d74706cc3d4c0148d43ce45f1ea8be7646f"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The RESET bit clears the basic core and FIFO circuits when LOCK is 0, and, set by a chip reset, holds the part in reset until the host clears it.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "682-685",
       "sha": "8535a6a357a9cc64bb0de8062f77ca4b9dc4bfb19c7079d6cf45d1c39390b239"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "A read of the DOR returns the byte last written, except on the XT, where the port reads 0xFF.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2650-2651",
       "sha": "acabf37d935a5cf0b2f4720c69ca3d7171404e4d044932749327abb16df96116"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2678",
       "sha": "241fe285b912b96cb626e2777b402f683b760b7d92a86fbe3ccc7cc07b3769b5"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "102",
     "on": "place",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "place",
     "text": "A write at port offset 0x02 passes the byte to fdc_baseio_w's DOR case, on_dor_change.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2595-2596",
       "sha": "7a73da9b4309a51894218b4159fbaed9edc842215ff550389c372d514e93d03a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "103",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "3",
     "text": "The FDC does not tristate INT or DRQ: a change of bit 3 activates or deactivates the IRQ line, which the Model 30 DIR returns as its DMA gate.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "1172-1175",
       "sha": "0fc725a7eb41432fb0c4423424b57e4ab494798b12161f30885ba0b89b19cca4"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "2422-2424",
       "sha": "3dc46c95d4bcd80c59571b5a612fd582bb8725da2ee3e1b8756beabc5598cc8b"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "1687-1694",
       "sha": "ca0c6b594422e4e52316afd66c34884e6a6e1d0de129a512c9e7398de440cfda"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "1860-1864",
       "sha": "29e6b88fe3e8ba6b6c6511137483300f7af4eb326564b313fe6c2a6425765080"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "104",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "differs",
     "row": "4",
     "text": "The FDC treats bit 2 as active low: clearing it resets the controller and it stays in reset while clear, not while the bit is set.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "1146-1157",
       "sha": "54afa639ada8827b3d93cb133495236684c065560bafd8aa649e28b7f97ac76e"
      },
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/floppy.cpp",
       "lines": "792-796",
       "sha": "d4fa2c9175ae51af96ed4fd44758f228d7d1d9a00651e53c48a0ccec7c8563f7"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
