   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The Main Status Register is read-only and is used for controlling command input and result output for all commands.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "787-795",
       "sha": "8cfc4ec10dfb9089d0e4861c4337f4a9d0a44efc7e15d4f01ee6c6bac2203145"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "RQM, printed ROM in the capture, (bit 7) says the host can transfer data, DIO (bit 6) gives the direction, and NON-DMA (bit 5) marks a polled execution phase.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "788-790",
       "sha": "4004351cbc00f65915a9ebfc17e60f028595b512c6395c352903053673c17ec8"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "796-805",
       "sha": "a300d4f4a1f4fcfe150bcbe70afa075731ebd7f7461ef1621bd8fb619b56c121"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "read",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bit 4 (command busy) is set while a command is in progress, and bits 3 to 0 are the drive busy bits during a seek or a recalibrate.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:82077SL.raw.txt",
       "lines": "806-815",
       "sha": "469dbbbbc49b3ad56aa6548f718ef887a361b8bc4fd242b3731597cb8b508688"
      },
      {
